Runs made by hand after try.sh and measure.sh, copied verbatim. $S is the
scratch directory. Same machine: Apple M4 Pro, macOS 27.0.1, OpenSSH_10.3p1,
OrbStack 29.4.0 running the Host (Alpine 3.22.7, sshd OpenSSH_10.0p2, rsync 3.5.0).

===== which ciphers the hops negotiate (ssh -v)
--- inner (OpenSSH -> Gateway)
debug1: kex: algorithm: mlkem768x25519-sha256
debug1: kex: host key algorithm: ssh-ed25519
debug1: kex: server->client cipher: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com MAC: <implicit> compression: none
debug1: kex: client->server cipher: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com MAC: <implicit> compression: none
--- direct (OpenSSH -> sshd)
debug1: kex: algorithm: mlkem768x25519-sha256
debug1: kex: host key algorithm: ssh-ed25519
debug1: kex: server->client cipher: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com MAC: <implicit> compression: none
debug1: kex: client->server cipher: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com MAC: <implicit> compression: none
(x/crypto v0.58.0 has chacha20 assembly for arm64 but none for poly1305;
the Device Connection and the Gateway's own connection to the Host pick
aes128-gcm, x/crypto's first choice.)

===== Gateway CPU: x/crypto default ciphers (:47443) against AES-GCM only inside the Tunnel (:47445)
$ kokoproto server -listen 127.0.0.1:47445 -gateway-ciphers aes128-gcm@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
debug1: kex: client->server cipher: aes128-gcm@openssh.com MAC: <implicit> compression: none
