===== agent forwarding: only sent when ssh has an agent to forward
(a scratch ssh-agent at $S/agent.sock; the "Host *" stand-in sets IdentityAgent none)
$ ssh -v -F $C -A web1.koko 'echo "remote SSH_AUTH_SOCK=${SSH_AUTH_SOCK:-unset}"'
debug1: Sending command: echo "remote SSH_AUTH_SOCK=${SSH_AUTH_SOCK:-unset}"
remote SSH_AUTH_SOCK=unset
$ ssh -G -F $C -A web1.koko | grep -i forwardagent
forwardagent yes
$ ssh -v -F $C -o ForwardAgent=yes -o IdentityAgent=agent.sock web1.koko '...'
debug1: Requesting agent forwarding on channel 0 via auth-agent-req@openssh.com
debug1: Sending command: echo "remote SSH_AUTH_SOCK=${SSH_AUTH_SOCK:-unset}"
remote SSH_AUTH_SOCK=unset
server 10:19:24.668942 gateway web1: channel request "auth-agent-req@openssh.com" refused

