===== which errors survive ControlPersist on the user's ssh
$ ssh -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPersist=30 web9.koko true   # unknown name: koko tunnel's stderr
Connection closed by UNKNOWN port 65535
[exit 255]
$ ssh web2.koko true   # Host down, no ControlPersist
koko: cannot reach web2: dial tcp 127.0.0.1:47099: connect: connection refused
Connection closed by UNKNOWN port 65535
[exit 255]
$ ssh -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPersist=30 web2.koko true   # Host down: the Gateway's banner, in band
koko: cannot reach web2: dial tcp 127.0.0.1:47099: connect: connection refused
Connection closed by UNKNOWN port 65535
[exit 255]

===== first run of try.sh, not reproduced since
The -L check of the first try.sh run left its Device Connection open for
16 s after the SSH Session ended (server.log of that run:
"device connection 127.0.0.1:56114 (alice/laptop) closed after 16.174s",
session "ended after 1.072s"). Its trace was overwritten. Eight later runs
of the same steps (one in the second try.sh run, one by hand, six in a loop) closed it within 1 ms of ssh exiting.

===== revocation during an open SSH Session, rerun after koko tunnel waits for the Tunnel to drain
$ (sleep 2; kokoproto revoke -device alice/laptop) & ssh -tt web1.koko 'for i in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do echo tick $i; sleep 0.5; done'
tick 1
tick 2
tick 3
tick 4
tick 5

koko: the Device Session "alice/laptop" was revoked; this SSH Session is closed.

koko: the Device Connection to 127.0.0.1:47443 closed.
Connection to web1.koko closed by remote host.
Connection to web1.koko closed.
client_loop: send disconnect: Broken pipe
[exit 255]
